    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60174" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρουμ-ατικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for playing on a stringed
			instrument</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.352.2
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>): in a general sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ κ. μουσικὴ
				ἡ διὰ τῶν αὐλῶν</span> Suid.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄλυμπος; διάλεκτος κ.</span>
			 style <i>in playing</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1138b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξεις κρουσματικαί</span>
			sounds <i>of music</i>, i.e. <i>inarticulate</i> sounds without
			sense, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.36.3
			</span></i>.</div>
